WEBVTT

00:50.800 --> 00:55.346
DOONA!

01:19.370 --> 01:20.622
Would you allow it?

01:22.373 --> 01:25.043
What kind of question is that?

01:25.752 --> 01:27.462
If you want to perform, you should.

01:28.088 --> 01:29.839
I'd love to see you sing, you know?

01:32.050 --> 01:33.802
I would support you no matter what.

01:34.803 --> 01:36.971
I forget sometimes how naive you are.

01:42.936 --> 01:44.896
What if they say we can't be together?

01:45.730 --> 01:46.815
Then what?

01:48.775 --> 01:50.860
Given what's at stake,
no one's dumb enough

01:50.944 --> 01:52.904
to add a boyfriend to the equation.
You got it?

01:52.987 --> 01:55.323
Not the label, not even Doona.

01:58.201 --> 01:59.702
So who should leave who alone?

02:00.495 --> 02:01.538
Take a guess.

02:24.227 --> 02:27.230
EPISODE 9
DOONA!

02:27.313 --> 02:28.273
Thank you.

02:31.234 --> 02:32.735
CONGRATS ON THE COMEBACK!

02:32.819 --> 02:36.030
ALL OF MSA WISHES YOU SUCCESS
IN YOUR SOLO CAREER, DOONA!

02:38.324 --> 02:39.242
Ah!

02:44.080 --> 02:47.834
FROZEN WATER PIPE PREVENTION TIPS

02:55.049 --> 02:57.969
I moved.
I'll give you my new address.

02:59.345 --> 03:00.305
THE CONSTITUTION

03:00.388 --> 03:01.431
It's colder now.

03:02.056 --> 03:03.224
I hope you're staying warm.

03:03.308 --> 03:05.268
2022 LEVEL 5 OPEN COMPETITIVE RECRUITMENT

03:07.729 --> 03:09.731
We don't have any photos together.

03:10.648 --> 03:12.192
Let's take some when we have time.

03:12.275 --> 03:13.735
2. EXAM SCHEDULE BY JOB CATEGORY

03:25.038 --> 03:27.332
I love you! Doona!

03:27.415 --> 03:28.708
Look over here, please.

03:32.212 --> 03:34.714
- Hello.
- Hello. Here. I brought you a gift.

03:34.797 --> 03:37.258
- So sweet. Thank you.
- Yeah, oh my gosh. You're so pretty.

03:38.384 --> 03:40.220
These glasses are pretty cool.

03:40.303 --> 03:42.972
- You don't mind if I try them on, right?
- Um…

03:43.056 --> 03:45.099
Where do they
even sell these things?

03:47.477 --> 03:50.021
Hey there, can you find out
where these are from real quick?

03:50.647 --> 03:52.649
Oh, and see this guy to the door.

03:54.234 --> 03:55.360
Security, please.

03:59.906 --> 04:01.157
Yeah, you're a disgrace.

04:03.910 --> 04:07.038
IT'S SMOOTH ENOUGH
TO DOWN IN ONE!

04:13.086 --> 04:15.046
You seem pretty shy. What's your name?

04:16.297 --> 04:18.007
Doona, hello there.

04:27.475 --> 04:29.018
Are you serious?

04:33.648 --> 04:34.482
Is it…

04:35.275 --> 04:36.234
It couldn't be.

04:39.862 --> 04:41.906
TO SU-JIN FROM DOONA
GO, KOOK'S SEAFOOD HOUSE!

04:45.326 --> 04:46.577
Whoo!

04:51.082 --> 04:53.668
MINSONG TOGETHER FESTIVAL
OUTDOOR CONCERT, LEE DOONA

04:55.128 --> 04:57.964
I'm so busy preparing
for the end of the semester.

05:07.932 --> 05:09.517
I really miss you.

05:26.451 --> 05:30.038
It feels like…
we're in two different worlds.

05:42.216 --> 05:43.509
She is so pretty!

05:52.935 --> 05:56.064
For us to have met
and to sit side by side

05:56.147 --> 05:57.940
feels purely by chance.

05:59.984 --> 06:02.236
Yes, we just finished,
and we're on the road.

06:03.237 --> 06:04.155
About an hour?

06:05.823 --> 06:07.450
The article's out the day after tomorrow.

06:07.533 --> 06:09.410
It's all been confirmed
with the team in Japan,

06:09.494 --> 06:11.120
so keep it under wraps until then.

06:34.936 --> 06:37.146
I feel angry today
for some reason.

06:47.990 --> 06:49.575
CRAM SCHOOL

06:51.869 --> 06:52.954
It's snowing.

06:53.996 --> 06:56.040
The semester ends in a few days.

06:58.292 --> 07:00.461
And my tutoring job ends soon too.

07:31.451 --> 07:34.996
It's cold out, but I haven't
seen that street cat Nana around.

07:35.705 --> 07:37.623
I'll look for her again tonight.

08:21.834 --> 08:23.294
Are you finished for the day?

08:24.670 --> 08:26.047
Want something to eat?

08:38.559 --> 08:39.560
Cheers.

08:47.693 --> 08:49.320
So you must've called a lot.

08:50.071 --> 08:50.905
Not really, no.

08:53.282 --> 08:54.158
Oh, really?

08:55.743 --> 08:57.453
I was sure you were worried sick.

08:58.496 --> 08:59.705
Well, that's good, then.

09:09.257 --> 09:11.884
They took my cell away,
so I couldn't message you at all.

09:12.552 --> 09:14.428
In fact, I barely snuck out tonight.

09:17.890 --> 09:21.269
Well, that's good, and…
you don't have to explain at all.

09:22.395 --> 09:25.398
I know you were…
born to be singing up on the stage.

09:29.235 --> 09:30.236
You'll do great.

09:38.327 --> 09:39.328
Is everything…

09:41.330 --> 09:42.790
okay with us, Won-jun?

09:46.836 --> 09:48.045
I have to serve soon.

09:54.010 --> 09:55.011
Oh yeah?

10:00.891 --> 10:01.851
Well, that's great.

10:02.351 --> 10:04.437
At least that will help time pass quickly.

10:15.531 --> 10:18.242
My agency treats me as if I'm crazy.

10:19.035 --> 10:20.244
They won't let me near a phone,

10:20.328 --> 10:23.372
and I can't even go to the bathroom
without someone chaperoning me.

10:23.456 --> 10:25.041
They're scared I'll run away again.

10:25.791 --> 10:27.335
It's all so unnecessary.

10:30.087 --> 10:32.506
I guess I understand
why they're like this. Hmm.

10:54.987 --> 10:57.239
So, um, given the situation
with where we are,

10:57.740 --> 10:59.950
it'll be another two years max
I won't be here.

11:00.451 --> 11:02.078
Do you think you can handle that?

11:03.037 --> 11:06.415
Once I'm well established,
my private life won’t matter then.

11:07.667 --> 11:08.626
After that, we can date.

11:08.709 --> 11:10.086
You don't need to, uh…

11:17.677 --> 11:18.969
Don't worry about me.

11:35.069 --> 11:36.862
You wanna give up just like that?

11:37.363 --> 11:38.322
Seriously?

11:39.448 --> 11:40.741
Isn't that what you were saying?

11:42.368 --> 11:43.953
No, I wasn't saying that.

11:49.834 --> 11:51.085
Well, that's what I'm saying.

11:54.839 --> 11:56.799
I think I wanna break up with you.

12:27.913 --> 12:31.542
So when I was a washed-up has-been,
you never had a problem with us dating.

12:31.625 --> 12:34.003
Now, 'cause I'm a star, you can't take it?

12:34.086 --> 12:36.338
Seriously,
what difference does it make, Won-jun?

12:39.049 --> 12:41.385
When I met with him last night,
do you know what I said?

12:42.219 --> 12:43.679
I told him you and I were dating

12:44.555 --> 12:46.474
and we're not about to let it end!

12:52.271 --> 12:53.981
Because I want you in my life.

12:55.566 --> 12:57.860
We've already gotten this far,
so why end it now?

13:00.946 --> 13:03.073
I don't understand what changed for you.

13:04.241 --> 13:06.535
So what's the point of me holding on?

13:08.120 --> 13:09.830
What could you have been going through

13:11.040 --> 13:12.208
compared to me?

13:13.042 --> 13:15.169
You were the one
who said I should go back.

13:16.462 --> 13:18.672
You said you wanted to see me sing.

13:32.228 --> 13:33.813
It's you who's letting go.

13:35.356 --> 13:37.566
You're the one
that's breaking your promise.

13:38.067 --> 13:40.945
You're running away from this
because you don't have the guts.

13:41.737 --> 13:43.614
You're leaving like all they all did.

13:46.242 --> 13:47.910
You're no different from the rest, okay?

13:51.622 --> 13:52.623
Am I right?

13:56.627 --> 13:57.628
Am I right?

14:04.134 --> 14:05.219
Apparently.

17:05.399 --> 17:06.567
Yeah, that's good.

17:09.361 --> 17:10.195
Action!

18:13.050 --> 18:13.884
I'VE MOVED

18:13.967 --> 18:14.802
I MISS YOU

18:14.885 --> 18:16.804
IT FEELS LIKE
WE'RE IN TWO DIFFERENT WORLDS

18:16.887 --> 18:19.848
FOR US TO HAVE MET AND TO SIDE BY SIDE
FEELS PURELY BY CHANCE

18:27.981 --> 18:29.399
So, what is dating?

18:29.983 --> 18:31.777
Dating is a muscle.

18:32.945 --> 18:34.279
Muscle!

18:37.032 --> 18:38.033
Uh…

18:39.493 --> 18:40.410
Muscle.

18:41.161 --> 18:42.579
Here's how to think of it.

18:42.663 --> 18:45.791
We've all been torn down
at some point in life, haven't we?

18:46.542 --> 18:49.336
Being torn down, as well as feeling pain,

18:49.419 --> 18:51.421
is necessary for building muscle.

18:51.505 --> 18:52.714
Oh.

18:52.798 --> 18:54.633
In fact, that's how we get stronger.

18:54.716 --> 18:56.218
DATING = MUSCLE

18:56.301 --> 18:58.762
Yes, even your heart may bulk up.

18:59.805 --> 19:02.099
Bulking… uh…

19:03.100 --> 19:04.226
bulking up your heart.

19:05.769 --> 19:07.813
So, everyone, dating is what again?

19:07.896 --> 19:09.231
It's a muscle.

19:09.314 --> 19:11.483
Louder. Tell me, what is dating again?

19:11.567 --> 19:13.068
It's a muscle!

19:13.152 --> 19:15.070
- What is it?
- It's a muscle!

19:15.154 --> 19:16.572
One last time.

19:16.655 --> 19:18.740
- It's a muscle!
- It's a muscle!

19:18.824 --> 19:21.869
You can do it! Yes, we can all
have love in our lives again.

19:21.952 --> 19:24.413
Just bulk up your heart! Yeah!

19:24.496 --> 19:25.581
Yeah!

19:25.664 --> 19:29.001
Let's all bulk up for… our love!

19:29.084 --> 19:30.335
Seo Yun-taek!

19:52.149 --> 19:53.901
Hey!

19:53.984 --> 19:55.444
Hey!

20:00.782 --> 20:03.911
Get up and eat breakfast.
I have to leave for work pretty soon.

20:10.167 --> 20:12.961
- Hurry up, huh?
- All right.

20:37.986 --> 20:39.196
I'm off to work.

20:41.198 --> 20:43.492
Ah, you're up early,
given how much you drank last night.

20:43.575 --> 20:45.994
- Yeah, I meant to go home and sleep.
- Hot, hot!

20:46.078 --> 20:48.664
I'll do that. You should grab
a protein bar or something.

20:53.418 --> 20:55.712
This one's for you. This one's for you.

20:57.172 --> 20:58.882
- And don't forget this!
- Thank you.

21:01.093 --> 21:02.886
- I'll get going!
- Have a good day.

21:04.763 --> 21:05.847
Okay, bye for now.

21:08.767 --> 21:10.727
Her job's going well, huh?

21:11.228 --> 21:14.273
Who would've thought…
that I-ra'd take a desk job.

21:14.356 --> 21:16.066
Or that I'd actually live with a girl!

21:16.650 --> 21:18.735
Yeah, that's weird.

21:18.819 --> 21:20.821
I'm not sure I'll ever get used to that.

21:22.364 --> 21:24.032
I gotta head out.
Take your time, all right?

21:24.116 --> 21:25.117
Thanks.

21:40.465 --> 21:42.217
- Hey, wait for us.
- Won-jun!

21:43.385 --> 21:45.053
- Hello.
- Hey.

21:54.771 --> 21:56.898
HANG IN THERE!
MAYBE DREAM SWEET WILL VISIT?

21:56.982 --> 21:59.109
TO SU-JIN FROM DOONA
GO, KOOK'S SEAFOOD HOUSE!

22:08.118 --> 22:11.788
The people at the Oseong Apartment
are saying they asked for pickled ginger.

22:11.872 --> 22:13.540
- They want it now.
- Huh?

22:15.792 --> 22:18.837
It wasn't on their order.
What are they saying?

22:23.300 --> 22:25.677
Uh, hi. I'm calling you
from Su-jin's Seafood House.

22:25.761 --> 22:27.637
You just complained about an order here?

22:27.721 --> 22:30.766
Just so you know, if you want ginger,
you have to order it on its own.

22:35.270 --> 22:37.022
Okay, it'll be a bit longer.

22:38.357 --> 22:39.191
I'll take it.

22:39.274 --> 22:42.444
Won-jun, I think they're messing with us
'cause you look like a pushover.

22:42.527 --> 22:45.030
- I'll deal with this.
- No, I can handle it. Give it here.

22:45.113 --> 22:46.448
Hey, I said I'll go, okay?

22:47.157 --> 22:49.034
You should chill with Jin-ju.

22:49.117 --> 22:50.118
What?

22:50.744 --> 22:51.578
Over here.

22:54.247 --> 22:55.290
Oh.

22:55.832 --> 22:59.878
I was starting to wonder
if you were even going to notice.

22:59.961 --> 23:01.505
You didn't feel me glaring?

23:01.588 --> 23:03.840
So, uh, when did you get back?

23:03.924 --> 23:05.509
Um…

23:06.009 --> 23:07.928
You should sit down.

23:09.679 --> 23:12.933
This is the desert in Las Vegas.
Check these out.

23:13.016 --> 23:15.811
- What are those? Boulders?
- Exactly. Aren't they pretty?

23:15.894 --> 23:18.897
Wow, that's really cool.

23:18.980 --> 23:20.649
- And here's Times Square.
- I recognize that.

23:20.732 --> 23:22.859
Wait, that's where they
drop the ball for the new year.

23:22.943 --> 23:26.154
- Right, that's exactly it.
- I wish I could've gone.

23:26.238 --> 23:27.781
And here are my friends from Brazil.

23:28.407 --> 23:30.575
So this guy is an amazing photographer.

23:30.659 --> 23:31.910
He's seriously awesome.

23:31.993 --> 23:32.994
Oh.

23:33.078 --> 23:35.622
He's a good-looking dude.

23:35.705 --> 23:37.457
They took this
on my way to school.

23:37.541 --> 23:39.876
And this is the restaurant
across from where I was staying.

23:39.960 --> 23:42.003
I'm there every day.
The food's seriously so good!

23:42.087 --> 23:44.798
- It's called Habibi?
- It is.

23:45.298 --> 23:48.301
- The weather in Brazil is just amazing.
- Ah. It looks awesome.

23:49.219 --> 23:52.347
- Oh, and look at this here.
- Wow. That looks amazing.

23:52.431 --> 23:54.641
Oh, I wanna go one day.

23:54.724 --> 23:57.144
- I'll start cleaning up. You keep talking.
- Okay.

23:57.811 --> 23:59.563
Ah, here's I-ra's parents' place.

23:59.646 --> 24:03.024
It was hard to find a place in Brazil,
so that's where I did a homestay.

24:03.733 --> 24:06.695
I originally went to visit.
Who knew I'd stay so long?

24:09.072 --> 24:09.948
Oops.

24:13.869 --> 24:15.495
Um…

24:16.663 --> 24:19.666
Uh, Doona had a concert in Brazil,
so I went and saw her sing.

24:20.625 --> 24:21.460
Hmm.

24:24.004 --> 24:25.297
What are you doing tonight?

24:25.380 --> 24:28.091
Uh, my sister and I are hanging out.

24:28.175 --> 24:30.385
- She's picking me up later.
- Cool.

24:34.806 --> 24:35.724
Hmm.

24:43.565 --> 24:48.987
SU-JIN'S SEAFOOD HOUSE (DELIVERY-ONLY)

25:32.364 --> 25:35.200
CONGRATS ON THE 4-YEAR ANNIVERSARY
OF YOUR DEBUT AS A SOLO ARTIST!

26:16.533 --> 26:19.661
LOVE AND DO WHAT YOU WILL

26:33.091 --> 26:35.552
So, is the house being demolished?
Have you heard anything?

26:36.386 --> 26:37.345
This house?

26:38.346 --> 26:41.558
I'm pretty sure that the landlord is gonna
remodel the whole thing for her son.

26:41.641 --> 26:43.935
He's getting married,
so it'll be a wedding gift.

26:44.686 --> 26:47.480
Ah, whoever that man is, I'm so jealous.

26:47.564 --> 26:51.610
Does that mean this is the last time
we'll all be here together like this?

26:51.693 --> 26:53.320
That's so depressing.

26:53.403 --> 26:54.571
Yeah, it is.

26:55.238 --> 26:57.532
Let's cheers.
It's been a while, everyone. Yep.

26:58.825 --> 27:00.410
Ah! Doona's missing here.

27:01.494 --> 27:05.081
It's not a full family reunion
if Doona isn't here to celebrate with us.

27:05.165 --> 27:06.625
Ah, Doona should've--

27:06.708 --> 27:09.628
You should eat more veggies
if you wanna stay healthy.

27:09.711 --> 27:11.713
How about we toast to everyone's health?

27:11.796 --> 27:13.632
- To everyone's health!
- To everyone's health!

27:13.715 --> 27:14.549
Cheers!

27:21.056 --> 27:24.017
- You aren't drinking much. How come?
- Oh, I have an interview in the morning.

27:24.100 --> 27:25.185
You do?

27:27.854 --> 27:29.939
It's down to the last stage.

27:30.482 --> 27:31.691
Are you serious?

27:31.775 --> 27:33.276
Nice! That's great!

27:33.360 --> 27:35.945
- Yeah, Won-jun!
- Congrats, man!

27:36.029 --> 27:39.199
Congratulations! Aw, that's my boy!

27:39.282 --> 27:41.451
Seriously, though, dang.
How are you still single?

27:41.534 --> 27:44.537
- What a waste this is. Am I right?
- You should've told us about it, huh?

27:47.707 --> 27:50.043
Ugh! This guy doesn't change!

27:50.126 --> 27:52.170
Why do you always keep stuff to yourself?

27:52.253 --> 27:55.298
- What else are you hiding?
- Let's see how the interview goes first.

27:55.382 --> 27:57.592
Knowing you,
you won't tell us till next year.

27:58.593 --> 27:59.969
I'll tell you either way, then.

28:00.929 --> 28:02.764
- Knock on wood.
- Knock on wood.

28:02.847 --> 28:05.058
- Don't jinx yourself!
- Knock on wood, everyone.

28:05.141 --> 28:07.936
- Congratulations!
- Cheers!

28:08.019 --> 28:10.563
It's been ages
since we've had Jin-ju with us.

28:10.647 --> 28:14.192
Let's after-party at our house,
or else you're a traitor if you bail.

28:14.275 --> 28:16.736
- It's because of my interview.
- Come on. Get in.

28:16.820 --> 28:19.406
- Won-jun, you're not coming, right?
- Next time, I promise.

28:19.489 --> 28:21.241
Okay, bye.
Call us when you get it.

28:21.324 --> 28:24.619
- Call us even if you don't.
- Won-jun, you're gonna get that job.

28:24.703 --> 28:26.287
- Won-jun!
- See you later.

28:26.371 --> 28:27.664
- Bye.
- Bye.

28:27.747 --> 28:28.581
Bye.

28:35.797 --> 28:36.631
Hmm.

30:51.099 --> 30:51.975
Hello there.

30:56.855 --> 30:58.481
I thought you had gone.

31:00.066 --> 31:01.276
I left my jacket inside.

31:02.694 --> 31:04.863
Oh, um… you should go get it.

32:00.084 --> 32:02.795
- So, how is everyone?
- Good.

32:09.844 --> 32:11.012
They're all doing well.

32:14.307 --> 32:15.892
Have you listened to my music?

33:29.424 --> 33:30.425
Lee Won-jun!

33:31.050 --> 33:33.094
Hey!

33:40.560 --> 33:44.480
"Take care of yourself"? That's all
you have to say to me after all this time?

33:44.564 --> 33:46.399
Well, I'm sorry.

33:48.276 --> 33:49.402
Let's talk inside.

34:06.836 --> 34:08.421
How are you so calm about this?

34:09.213 --> 34:10.339
Is that how it looks?

34:11.299 --> 34:12.884
Do you have any idea

34:14.093 --> 34:15.887
how much I needed you then?

34:16.804 --> 34:19.057
You're the only reason
I'm alive right now.

34:19.599 --> 34:20.641
Back then, I…

34:22.185 --> 34:24.312
I despised myself so much I couldn't even

34:25.063 --> 34:26.189
get up most days.

34:27.106 --> 34:30.443
I no longer worried about
what life had in store… until we met.

34:30.526 --> 34:32.320
Yeah, well, things are different now.

34:33.571 --> 34:35.114
You're right. It is different,

34:35.698 --> 34:37.200
'cause now I don't hate myself.

34:38.034 --> 34:39.535
I'm better than I've ever been.

34:39.619 --> 34:41.329
I'm no longer unstable or selfish.

34:41.412 --> 34:43.539
I'm sleeping well, and work's going great.

34:44.332 --> 34:46.667
And people stay by my side,
even without you.

34:48.669 --> 34:49.879
So now,

34:50.505 --> 34:52.048
I'll never need a man in my life again.

34:54.175 --> 34:55.176
I already know.

35:02.266 --> 35:04.393
So this time it's your turn to beg.

35:06.813 --> 35:07.772
Tell me you're sorry.

35:09.690 --> 35:11.067
And what you did was wrong.

35:16.114 --> 35:17.073
I'm sorry.

35:18.783 --> 35:20.201
I should've gone after you.

35:21.702 --> 35:22.912
Tell me you regret it.

35:24.330 --> 35:25.706
Say you regret it!

35:31.546 --> 35:32.672
I regret it.

35:35.383 --> 35:37.135
I should've fought for us. I was wrong.

35:39.053 --> 35:41.013
Now just leave me alone, okay?

35:43.641 --> 35:44.517
I'm begging you.

35:48.521 --> 35:49.814
I really missed you.

36:00.408 --> 36:01.868
I really missed you too.

36:22.346 --> 36:25.474
2027 NATIONAL CIVIL SERVANT LEVEL 5
OPEN COMPETITIVE RECRUITMENT EXAM

36:27.560 --> 36:29.896
